  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 523.02 Criteria for Approval of Dredging Projects",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 523.02 Criteria for Approval of Dredging Projects. In addition to meeting the requirements established in Env-Wt 300, the department shall approve a dredging project only if the dredging project is:\n\n(a) Necessary to maintain an existing navigable passageway, fire pond, or infrastructure facility;\n\n(b) Part of a previously-constructed maintenance dredge project that is not abandoned or an active man-made pond; or\n\n(c) Part of an approved project for the maintenance of a pre-existing dug-in boathouse.\n\nSource. #12805, eff 12-15-19; ss by #14389, eff 9-25-25, EXPIRES: 9-25-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt500.html"
